<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW Environment</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss_en_environment</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss_en_environment" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-11798?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss_en_environment" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>COP31: No agreement on climate science, disinformation spreading</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d78217a06cb155608de729ba4199d86060d3ca21cbeceed34c962f6ea707e90f</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-no-agreement-on-climate-science-disinformation-spreading/a-80004894--cd9d23743160.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-no-agreement-on-climate-science-disinformation-spreading/a-80004894?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Attacks on climate science and disinformation risk delaying key measures at COP31 in Antalya. As the UN climate talks draw to a close, how will that affect efforts to come to an agreement?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Have we missed our chance to stop climate change?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2f6d34d1072dd7a62fcc27648aa10eb4466f39ea7ff38fb6fa29ffc681c56d0</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/have-we-missed-our-chance-to-stop-climate-change/a-79986199--68173e73a2c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/have-we-missed-our-chance-to-stop-climate-change/a-79986199?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From record-breaking heat to devastating floods and wildfires, the warning signs are everywhere. Can rising temperatures still be brought under control?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda minister at COP31: 'We need a just transition'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf84dfcab8583577f5ce028874235ba3809ac32e1f0fdc308a61aa1d2594e00b</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209--312e033bb073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Funding from wealthy countries to help deal with the impacts of climate change hasn't materialized, says Uganda's environment minister. The East African country is hoping oil and carbon credits will help boost finances.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>No mention of fossil fuels in latest COP31 draft deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:89d94f791828bfd7975d420e3ef83bc6f911a623b7c069bb04223c6fa1035481</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-mention-of-fossil-fuels-in-latest-cop31-draft-deal/a-79992394--36cfb19df8f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-mention-of-fossil-fuels-in-latest-cop31-draft-deal/a-79992394?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of the most fraught debates at the UN climate talks in Turkey has revolved around the future of coal, oil and gas. Now, all mention of fossil fuels has been removed from the summit's new draft agreement.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>How a green economy could help reverse climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c05e8fd0f68e92cbb2f8642dd35819fe9f420aa4be272247eb171125ffa13595</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-green-economy-could-help-reverse-climate-change/a-79874576--23cc55e56fdb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-green-economy-could-help-reverse-climate-change/a-79874576?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Green growth promises a future in which economies thrive without destroying the environment. But is this vision realistic?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>COP31 draft deal calls for 'immediate' shift away from fossil fuels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6b9287270f0a5a3f71e06e07cd74695c5544834bf8af80d06e5f6478283223b</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705--2a7f1bfc2c85.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-draft-deal-calls-for-immediate-shift-away-from-fossil-fuels/a-79960705?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The preliminary agreement at UN climate talks in Turkey calls for a rapid reduction of planet-warming emissions and at least $120 billion to help countries adapt to climate change.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Can a 'coalition of the willing' create momentum for a fossil fuel phaseout?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:003023ae68ddf83ceccac60f47c305cc789417d643eb86fdc078ced9b910e630</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T08:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748--1f05ab68dfcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-a-coalition-of-the-willing-create-momentum-for-a-fossil-fuel-phaseout/a-79926748?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In April, about 60 countries held an unprecedented meeting in Colombia to work out a plan to slowly quit oil, coal and gas. How influential is this coalition at the COP31 climate summit?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>What's going on with the polar vortex?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbfe5cb4baee1bbc2dacdbf6b214cd45173a0cd5b903be46c8a1f93d08aaab2c</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105--6a28f0640609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-s-going-on-with-the-polar-vortex/a-79943105?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Observations show the ring of fierce winds that rotate at the Earth's North Pole has changed direction. Scientists say it's a historic disruption and the earliest reversal on record. What could it mean for the weather?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Could lack of money sink TFFF rainforest fund before it even launches?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0adb0ad5293396ef5b6c2efc8e0e64f34cc4d65941e05a8851ccbbe8cd34a145</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673--227abf2cebee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-lack-of-money-sink-tfff-rainforest-fund-before-it-even-launches/a-79878673?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TFFF rainforest fund aims to make forest conservation more profitable than deforestation. But a lack of money may prevent it from getting off the ground.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>What are fossil fuels?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df7591860b8331691705b2a8eaac8a33f5f70957f91f1e0d13053710dee9ba99</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540--1920eabf4714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-are-fossil-fuels/a-67970540?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">They are in our shampoo bottles, power our cars and heat our homes. But what actually are fossil fuels, and why do they matter?</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Can global leaders put their money where their mouth is on climate?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dfdffdcf3fe9a9a631b38e03fa68649041ed838a4d4c51fc7d4dd1d8167400c</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-global-leaders-put-their-money-where-their-mouth-is-on-climate/a-79918744--b2fe82b3dbb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-global-leaders-put-their-money-where-their-mouth-is-on-climate/a-79918744?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World leaders warn that geopolitical divisions are distracting from the climate crisis as negotiations focus on clean energy and financing, while Iran calls for compensation for war-related environmental damage.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5be1a2f1e3422de52c92feb8a3ee8b9910cd379de34e914e2984ea0d6fd50d01</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Why electrification is the climate game changer we need</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:36565c56b44b252e1f8638ce7dedd358bc007d13f79c5bee12b70e19923eebd5</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979--0dbca6445640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-electrification-is-the-climate-game-changer-we-need/a-79615979?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From EVs and electric buses on the road, heat pumps warming homes and solar panels powering appliances, the shift to electrifying tech is already in full swing. But what exactly does "electrification" mean?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Australia push for fossil fuel exit at UN talks?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75e87b7cac2726750ed53caf3b3a1673513070a3c2c922099feec1182798c093</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066--e866c53d355a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-australia-push-for-fossil-fuel-exit-at-un-talks/a-79782066?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The heat is on Australia as chief negotiator at the COP31 UN climate conference to forge a path away from coal and gas, and to protect Pacific neighbors facing rising sea levels.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war oil shock drives dip in global emissions, study shows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a6f3b6c6490c26439bf9c991cc89b3d37b6e984facd6d0a149f9beced869c3f</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T03:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937--fec20d5dba18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-oil-shock-drives-dip-in-global-emissions-study-shows/a-79905937?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Global carbon emissions are expected to fall slightly in 2026, but not because of major progress on climate action. Instead, it's high energy prices following the US attack on Iran that's driving the trend.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>As COP31 Antalya kicks off, can world move beyond big promises?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef400cffd7fe1682b1cbfdf8aae12f5b7d7351cef2945d76bf72ca9ce7c4bf92</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T05:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366--3ff0bee69cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-cop31-antalya-kicks-off-can-world-move-beyond-big-promises/a-79661366?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Droughts, floods and extreme heat are upping the pressure on delegates at the UN climate talks in Antalya, Turkey. Can countries move beyond pledges to concrete action?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Preparing for 45C: How Germany tests its crisis response</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8203d4d766f0a62be5f9ee8e04f836c6f2039223f8343e1cbadcae25a921274</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/preparing-for-45c-how-germany-tests-its-crisis-response/a-79865768--9e044f771cb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/preparing-for-45c-how-germany-tests-its-crisis-response/a-79865768?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A record heat wave. Five years of drought. A nation under pressure. Germany is running its biggest joint crisis exercise to date to test how authorities would cope with an escalating climate emergency.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>LA communities kick out Big Oil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e59bb19146973d018365e9f453c3d7b6127c9b20a520fb1eb229445a4da1a27</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T14:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843--72df9d2c6283.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/la-communities-kick-out-big-oil/a-79830843?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After years of advocacy from residents and legal battles with Big Oil, Los Angeles voted to ban drilling and phase out oil extraction in the city. It's the first city in the United States to kick the oil industry out.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Can we regrow damaged seagrass meadows?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7db612cf544e423cc585521902a9c8c61ed9cb40107ea20f2e7efd44808bd2f</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925--ee57fe9c850d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-we-regrow-damaged-seagrass-meadows/a-79617925?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seagrass protects coasts, shelters thousands of species and stores CO2. But some 30% of this valuable ecosystem has disappeared since the late 19th century. Can we bring it back?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>EU moves to loosen rules on pesticide use as experts sound the alarm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3af97ad18842848ecc924e15dda4baf39083a39af8b6843d4a0a24195741bd12</id><updated>2026-11-22T07:08:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422--0c5446a2b9ff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-moves-to-loosen-rules-on-pesticide-use-as-experts-sound-the-alarm/a-79646422?maca=en-rss_en_environment-22607-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Union wants to relax rules for pesticides, saying it will be easier for farmers to adopt more environmentally friendly options. But health and environmental experts say the risks are far too great.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry></feed>
